From: Terry Gong <terry.gong@bytedance.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bitbake: tolerate read-only /proc when disabling network

Some sandboxed build environments (containers, restricted mount
namespaces) present /proc as a read-only mount even for root. In that
case bb.utils.disable_network() succeeds in unshare(CLONE_NEWUSER|
CLONE_NEWNET) but then aborts with:

    OSError: [Errno 30] Read-only file system: '/proc/self/uid_map'

which fails every do_unpack. There is nothing bitbake can do about the
sandbox, but the failure mode is unnecessary: the network is already
unshared inside the new namespace, so if we cannot write the uid/gid
maps we simply lose the ability to keep the original uid, which is not
required for do_unpack.

Catch OSError from those writes and downgrade to a debug log message,
matching the existing behavior for the "unshare not supported" path.

Apply on top of poky/master (bitbake 2.12).

diff --git a/poky/bitbake/lib/bb/utils.py b/poky/bitbake/lib/bb/utils.py
--- a/poky/bitbake/lib/bb/utils.py
+++ b/poky/bitbake/lib/bb/utils.py
@@ -1714,12 +1714,16 @@ def disable_network(uid=None, gid=None):
     ret = libc.unshare(CLONE_NEWNET | CLONE_NEWUSER)
     if ret != 0:
         logger.debug("System doesn't support disabling network without admin privs")
         return
-    with open("/proc/self/uid_map", "w") as f:
-        f.write("%s %s 1" % (uid, uid))
-    with open("/proc/self/setgroups", "w") as f:
-        f.write("deny")
-    with open("/proc/self/gid_map", "w") as f:
-        f.write("%s %s 1" % (gid, gid))
+    try:
+        with open("/proc/self/uid_map", "w") as f:
+            f.write("%s %s 1" % (uid, uid))
+        with open("/proc/self/setgroups", "w") as f:
+            f.write("deny")
+        with open("/proc/self/gid_map", "w") as f:
+            f.write("%s %s 1" % (gid, gid))
+    except OSError as e:
+        logger.debug("Skipping network disable: cannot write /proc uid/gid maps (%s)" % e)
+        return
